VERDICT: FINDINGS
CANDIDATE: 5dc1e7f2f147d087097e0799c96a672eee02d44b
FINDING task-detail-datecompleted blocking: The custom `custom/Espo/Custom/Resources/layouts/Task/detail.json` drops the core `dateCompleted` field from the Task detail view for every user. The WO asked for nothing like this: item 3 only adds a collapsed Legacy panel and `meetingType` on Meeting. It breaks existing core behaviour, and follow-ups (item 5, R9 "original … dates") need it. The test suite also locks the omission in: `activity_policy.CORE_FIELDS["Task"]` leaves out `dateCompleted`, so `rule_layouts` rejects the fix. | evidence: `python3 -c json.dumps(Task/detail)` → rows name, parent / status, priority / dateStart, dateEnd / reminders / description / attachments, then Legacy. No `dateCompleted`. `dc.py` (scratch) appended the row `[{"name":"dateCompleted"},false]` to the bundle → `rule_layouts` = `["Task/detail: unknown field 'dateCompleted'"]`; `"dateCompleted" in CORE_FIELDS["Task"]` → False. The PL's comparison in the 10.0.12 image confirms core Task/detail has the field. | expected: Task/detail keeps every core field, including `dateCompleted` (put it back next to dateStart/dateEnd), and `CORE_FIELDS["Task"]` includes `dateCompleted` so the layout rule accepts it.
FINDING browser-ac3-ac7-unverified advisory: The WO says BROWSER: yes, and AC3–AC7 (History/Activities panels, Staff cannot edit an archived body, calendar, "My open tasks", sfId duplicate rejection) are browser or live-stack behaviour. I could not run them here: no EspoCRM stack, no headless browser (`import playwright` → ModuleNotFoundError, no chromium/firefox), and I did not use the Docker socket. The candidate also adds no `tests/acceptance` checks for AC3–AC7, so the operator has to do them by hand. | evidence: `which chromium google-chrome firefox node` → none; `git diff --stat 57d93eb HEAD` → no change under tests/acceptance | expected: the operator runs AC3–AC7 on crm-dev with synthetic data. Ideally AC4 and AC7 get API-level acceptance tests.
FINDING email-address-links-unverified advisory: Not verified, since there is no Espo runtime. The hook guards the varchar attributes `from`, `to`, `cc`, `bcc`, `fromString` but not `replyTo` or the underlying address link attributes (e.g. `fromEmailAddressId`, `toEmailAddressesIds`). ER Manager keeps Email edit `all`. If 10.0.12 accepts those link ids directly on PUT, a Manager could change an archived email's addresses without tripping the guard. | evidence: hook PROTECTED_ATTRIBUTES = name, body, bodyPlain, isHtml, from, to, cc, bcc, fromString, dateSent, messageId, status; probe.py roles: ER Manager Email edit = all | expected: the operator confirms at AC4 that a Manager PUT of `toEmailAddressesIds`/`replyTo` on an Archived email is refused with 403, or the hook covers those attributes.
EVIDENCE:
- HEAD check: `git -C worktree rev-parse HEAD` = 5dc1e7f2f147d087097e0799c96a672eee02d44b. `git status --porcelain` was empty at the start and again at the end; HEAD was unchanged at the end.
- Full suite: `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -m unittest discover -s tests/unit` → Ran 307, OK. tests/acceptance → setUpModule ConfigError (needs CRM_ADMIN_* and a live stack), as expected for the operator stage.
- Non-vacuity against base: I took a `git archive` of base 57d93eb, overlaid the candidate's `tests/`, and ran it in scratch → FAILED (failures=9, errors=13). That covers test_email_edit_levels, unique sfId index, no-readOnly legacy fields and role fieldData coverage, among others.
- My mutation probes (probe.py) caught every one of these:
  - `readOnly` added to Email.sfId and to Task.sfOwnerId;
  - `readOnlyAfterCreate` removed from Call.sfId;
  - sfId index removed on each of Call, Meeting, Task and Email, and the index type changed to non-unique;
  - in the hook: `getFetched`→`get`; isAdmin exemption removed; username check removed (any API user exempt); wrong username `er-importer`; `body` dropped from the list; isNew guard removed; `throw`→`return`;
  - api_users.json renamed (hook and config out of sync);
  - "My open tasks" title lost; deployToTeams `["ER Staff"]` (nonexistent team);
  - meetingType made readOnly.
- Repo bundle: all activity rules hold.
- Decision table `archived_save_allowed`, 8 cases, all as expected:
  - new record → allowed;
  - Archived + Staff + body → denied;
  - Archived + parentId → allowed;
  - admin → allowed;
  - er-import → allowed;
  - Draft → allowed;
  - Archived + status → denied;
  - no change → allowed.
- Roles (roles.json):
  - Email edit: Staff no, Intake no, Manager all, Import all.
  - Staff, Intake and Manager: sfId read no/edit no on Call, Meeting, Task and Email; the other legacy fields read yes/edit no.
  - ER Import: yes/yes on all of them, plus create yes and edit all on Call, Meeting, Task and Email.
  - All legacy fields carry no `readOnly`; sfId has `readOnlyAfterCreate: true`.
- Unique index `{"type":"unique","columns":["sfId"]}` is present in the Call, Meeting, Task and Email entityDefs.
- Dashboard provisioning (prov.py, FakeEspo from the test suite):
  - run 1 without the flag: created 1, deployed [];
  - run 2: no writes, unchanged 1;
  - run 3 with `--deploy-dashboards`: only `POST DashboardTemplate/action/deployToTeam` to Enquiries with append False; still one template;
  - run 4 with the flag: no template writes, deploys again (documented as replacing the users' dashboards).
- `php -l` on the hook (PHP 8.4.27 is present in this sandbox) → No syntax errors. A copy with a deliberate error → Parse error, so the lint can fail.
- gitleaks: `gitleaks dir` on the worktree → no leaks; `gitleaks git --log-opts=57d93eb..HEAD` → no leaks.
- Browser and AC3–AC7: INCONCLUSIVE, because there is no browser tooling or stack (see the advisory finding).
- I started no servers or processes, so no ports are in use. All scratch files are in /srv/CRM/worktrees/.forge-scratch/CRM-005.
